        <h2>International Shipping: CIF vs FOB Terms</h2>
        <p>Understanding shipping terms determines your responsibilities and costs:</p>

        <h3>CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) Terms:</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Our responsibility:</strong> Equipment delivered to your nearest major port</li>
          <li><strong>Includes:</strong> Crating, container loading, ocean freight, marine insurance</li>
          <li><strong>Your responsibility:</strong> Port charges, customs clearance, inland transport</li>
          <li><strong>Typical cost:</strong> $3,500-$12,000 depending on destination and equipment size</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>FOB (Free on Board) Terms:</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Our responsibility:</strong> Equipment loaded on truck at our facility</li>
          <li><strong>Your responsibility:</strong> All shipping, insurance, and logistics</li>
          <li><strong>Lower price:</strong> You save shipping costs but handle all logistics</li>
          <li><strong>More complex:</strong> Requires your freight forwarder and shipping knowledge</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Container Requirements:</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>M30-M50:</strong> Single 20ft or 40ft container</li>
          <li><strong>M100:</strong> Single 40ft high-cube container</li>
          <li><strong>M200+:</strong> Multiple containers or break-bulk shipping</li>
          <li><strong>Professional crating:</strong> Secure packaging for ocean transport</li>
        </ul>

